From af3afb52e6d7fc48423fe83a4012641d453441d6 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: dianqk <dianqk@dianqk.net>
Date: Sat, 31 Oct 2026 21:08:49 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] arm64: dts: qcom: sdm660-xiaomi-clover: Use the full CPU
 frequency table

Drop the qcom,lut-max-microvolt limit, so cpufreq offers every entry of
the speed bin 1 OSM table: silver 1747.2 and 1843.2 MHz and gold 1958.4,
2150.4 and 2208 MHz in addition. These corners run above the 872 mV APM
threshold, where the OSM switches the memory arrays from VDD_MX to the
APC supply through the crossover corner, as programmed by the vendor
sequence. The CPRh stays in open loop.

Scope: Clover
Porting notes: Local device tree change (not upstream).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/sdm660-xiaomi-clover-common.dtsi | 7 -------
 1 file changed, 7 deletions(-)

diff --git a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/sdm660-xiaomi-clover-common.dtsi b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/sdm660-xiaomi-clover-common.dtsi
index 6cea3b0747..e4fdf01ac8 100644
--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/sdm660-xiaomi-clover-common.dtsi
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/sdm660-xiaomi-clover-common.dtsi
@@ -435,13 +435,6 @@ &cpu7 {
 };
 
 &cpufreq_hw {
-	/*
-	 * Keep the LUT entries that need the APC array supply (above the
-	 * 872 mV APM threshold) unused: silver up to 1536 MHz and gold up
-	 * to 1747.2 MHz.
-	 */
-	qcom,lut-max-microvolt = <868000>;
-
 	status = "okay";
 };
 
